WEBVTT

00:01:57.788 --> 00:02:01.246
“I have been in full harmony all my life
with the tides which have flowed

00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:05.579
on both sides of the Atlantic
against privilege and monopoly,”

00:02:05.621 --> 00:02:09.413
thus highlighting his virtue
as somebody commited to democracy.

00:02:09.746 --> 00:02:12.996
Much earlier, in his defense
of the poet Archias,

00:02:13.038 --> 00:02:15.746
Roman consul Cicero appealed 
to his own practical wisdom

00:02:15.788 --> 00:02:18.246
and expertise as a politician:

00:02:18.288 --> 00:02:20.788
“Drawn from my study
of the liberal sciences

00:02:20.829 --> 00:02:23.788
and from that careful training
to which I admit

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:26.871
that at no part of my life
have I ever been disinclined.”

00:02:27.121 --> 00:02:29.913
And finally, you can 
demonstrate disinterest

00:02:29.954 --> 00:02:33.038
or that you’re not motivated
by personal gain.